"In a Rapport, only a hn'tyon (knight) can declare someone a guest."
"Those who have declared intent to become knights may also grant guest right in their own house."
"Guests are exempt from swearing Privacy of the House."
"A guest may use the host family's summonarium to leave whenever they wish."
"A first guest is welcomed warmly; the highest-ranked member who met them then praises the host."
"The praise honors the host's wise decision that will enrich fellow knights' lives."
"A guest cottage holds a bowl of welcome whose fruits carry meaning, such as first meetings."
"A guest leaves gifts on a table in the mudroom and may clean the house's wevvi cups."
"Cleaning the cups shows willingness to share one's magic with the house."
"A hearthstone lit by a drop of Artonan blood honors shared kinship as children of the Mother."
"The host then serves wevvi from a cart in a formal circle."
"Guest cottages hold convenience rings for nonwizard guests and knights recovering from affixation."
